> > and donate. "Your devotion is rewarded."  And suddenly, *all* the
> > protection is back!
> >
> > I had no idea the game operated that way. So, why? Does the game record 
> > whether or not you are protected as a boolean intrinsic, and the amount of 
> > your protection as an integer?
> 
> how much protection did you get "back" exactly?  if you have *no* protection,
> you can get up to 4 (you get rn1(3,2)- namely 2 to 4 points of protection)-
> but there is no remembering things-- here is the relevant code:

Umm, yes there is. Gremlin theft clears HProtection (aka
u.uprops[PROTECTION].intrinsic)'s INTRINSIC bits, but leaves
u.ublessed alone. u.ublessed is only applied by find_ac() if any of
HProtection's INTRINSIC bits are set (in practice just FROMOUTSIDE,
since no race or role receives protection). Thus it's exactly as Kevin
surmises.

>         verbalize("Thy devotion has been rewarded.");
> 	if (!(HProtection & INTRINSIC))  {
> 	     HProtection |= FROMOUTSIDE;
>               if (!u.ublessed)  u.ublessed = rn1(3, 2);
>         } else u.ublessed++;

Note the if (!u.ublessed) requirement.

(The fact that failing this requirement after having lost protection
to a gremlin means you don't even get a single extra point, just the
effect of your existing u.ublessed back, is (along with the equivalent
divine boon code) inconsistent with eating rings of protection where
you _do_ earn the points, has been on my open bug report list for a
few years; it's therefore probable that the DevTeam are happy with the
way it's working, inconsistent though it might be.)

